NSDMI list-initialization with a null pointer constant fails overload
resolution ("does not uniquely resolve") when the class has both
rvalue-reference and nullptr_t constructors; the same initializer for
a local variable resolves fine.  From std::shared_ptr NSDMIs in
variable-sensitivity headers; blocks the abstract_environment dog-food
TU.
